Package: GDSAnnotator
Type: Package
Title: Whole-genome variant annotation data manipulation using GDS files
Version: 0.99.1
Depends: R (>= 4.6.0), gdsfmt (>= 1.32.0), SeqArray (>= 1.53.2)
Imports: methods, utils, IRanges, GenomicRanges, S4Vectors
Suggests: VariantAnnotation, BiocStyle, knitr, rmarkdown, testthat (>= 3.0.0)
Authors@R: c(person("Xiuwen", "Zheng", role=c("aut", "cre"),
        email="xiuwen.zheng@abbvie.com",
        comment=c(ORCID="0000-0002-1390-0708")),
        person("Yuantao (Raven)", "Chen", role="ctb"),
        person("Hufeng", "Zhou", role="ctb", email="hufengzhou@g.harvard.edu"))
Description: Fast and memory-efficient manipulation of whole-genome variant
        annotation data stored in Genomic Data Structure (GDS) files. FAVOR
        introduced the annotated GDS (aGDS) format, in which the FAVOR
        annotations of a study are added to its genotype GDS file. This
        package generalizes the format to annotation GDS files of any source,
        with or without genotypes. Annotation resources and annotator
        outputs, including FAVOR, gnomAD, Ensembl VEP and SnpEff, are
        converted into compact SeqArray-compatible GDS files with random
        access. Variants can be given as chr-pos-ref-alt strings, data
        frames, GRanges objects, VCF files or objects, or SeqArray GDS files.
        They are annotated by querying the annotation files, and the
        annotations can be written back into a genotype GDS file. Summary
        statistics of the variants and their annotations are computed in a
        single pass over a file and rendered as a VEP/SnpEff-like report.
        The package is intended for large-scale whole-genome sequencing
        studies.
